      "chapter": "equilibrium",
      "spoken": "At equilibrium, flow from Ready to In Use equals flow back. Zero point two times p equals zero point three times the quantity one minus p. So p is three fifths. That is exact; a finite power is only an approximation.",
      "coach": "At equilibrium, balance the two flows: 0.2p = 0.3(1 − p). Ready has exact probability 3/5.",
      "end": 103.885,
